Z||000001||avengador1||12-07-2001||07:15 PM||||A long block is an engine block with complete head assemblies attached and all it's internal components. The prices they are quoting seem reasonable if this is what they are trying to sell you. You basically are getting a new engine without all the external stuff like intake manifold, valve covers, oil pan, water pump,etc. At least this is what I remember. A short block is just the engine block with the crank bearings, and pistons. Hope this helps. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
